+# Hegel Property-Based Testing Report for `jiff`
+
+Scope: `crates/jiff` (v0.2.34). Hegel added as `hegeltest` 0.28.2 with the
+`jiff` feature. The pre-existing quickcheck property suite (19 properties)
+was ported to hegel per the porting reference, and 13 new properties were
+added. All tests live in the existing `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` blocks of the
+files whose code they test.
+
+Setup notes:
+
+- `cargo add --dev hegeltest --features jiff -p jiff` failed on jiff's
+  `rust-version = "1.70"` (hegeltest's MSRV is 1.86); retried with
+  `--ignore-rust-version` as the reference instructs. Upstreaming these tests
+  would raise the dev-dependency MSRV — maintainer's call.
+- A `[patch.crates-io] jiff = { path = "crates/jiff" }` entry was added to
+  the workspace `Cargo.toml`. Without it, hegeltest's `jiff` integration
+  resolves a *second* copy of jiff from crates.io and its generators produce
+  values of the wrong crate instance (nothing type-checks against the local
+  crate).
+- Even with the patch, hegel's typed jiff generators produce values of the
+  *extern* `jiff` crate (the self dev-dependency `jiff = { path = "." }`),
+  which inside jiff's own unit tests is a distinct crate instance from
+  `crate`. Tests that only exercise public API use `jiff::...` types and the
+  extras generators; ported tests that need crate internals
+  (`util::b` bounds, `Time::from_nanosecond`, `Span::to_invariant_duration`)
+  generate `crate` values from primitive draws instead.
+- The old `quickcheck::Arbitrary` impls and the quickcheck dev-dependency
+  were left in place: the impls are `#[cfg(test)]` library code that still
+  compiles against quickcheck, and removing them is an invasive change for
+  the maintainer. All `quickcheck::quickcheck! { ... }` property blocks were
+  replaced by hegel tests (coverage is a superset; nothing was dropped).
+
+## Properties tested
